{
  "id": "frequency-discrimination",
  "term": "frequency discrimination",
  "definition": "Frequency discrimination is the ability to tell apart stimuli that differ in frequency; in this packet, it refers to judging differences in higher spatial frequency in visual patterns. It is described in terms of a discrimination threshold, with lower thresholds indicating better discrimination, and the packet reports that this ability improves with age and with practice during the task.",
